---
import ProjectLayout from '../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro';
---

<ProjectLayout
  title="The Field of Seeds"
  subtitle="Thousands of light dandelions return to the lawn where the Seed Cathedral once stood."
  description="A physical-computing installation that replants light at the former site of Expo 2010's UK Pavilion."
  period="2024"
  kind="Physical Media & Computing Installation"
  status="Course project · team of three"
  role="Topic selection, concept definition & design, form design and circuit design"
  projectClass="portfolio-page--seeds"
  nextHref="/work/rooftop-garden"
  nextTitle="Rooftop Garden"
>
  <section class="project-hero project-hero--seeds">
    <img
      src="/pictures/work/field-of-seeds/fos-hero.png"
      alt="A field of light dandelions"
    />
    <p>The Seed Cathedral was dismantled. The memory stayed in the ground.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="portfolio-section">
    <div class="portfolio-section__head"><h2>The Seed Cathedral, Gone</h2></div>
    <p class="portfolio-copy portfolio-copy--flush">
      With its concept and form, the UK Pavilion's Seed Cathedral became one of the most memorable
      images of Expo 2010 Shanghai, leaving a unique impression on the city. After the Expo
      closed, the pavilion was dismantled, and its site is now a lawn.
    </p>
    <p class="portfolio-copy portfolio-copy--flush">
      This project makes a small attempt on that patch of green—so the city's Expo memory can keep
      spreading.
    </p>
    <figure class="project-figure project-figure--white">
      <img
        src="/pictures/work/field-of-seeds/fos-p2-1.png"
        alt="The UK Pavilion, the Seed Cathedral, Expo 2010 Shanghai"
      />
      <figcaption>The UK Pavilion — the Seed Cathedral — Expo 2010 Shanghai.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="portfolio-section portfolio-section--dark">
    <div class="portfolio-section__inner">
      <div class="portfolio-section__head"><h2>The Site</h2></div>
      <p class="portfolio-copy portfolio-copy--flush">
        The former Expo C zone is now Expo Culture Park—the only large green park in Shanghai's
        central urban area, still serving the city for rest and landscape.
      </p>
      <p class="portfolio-copy portfolio-copy--flush">
        The former UK Pavilion site lies between the Shanghai Italy Center (former Italy Pavilion)
        and the Rodin Art Center (former France Pavilion): a riverside artificial lawn with trees.
      </p>
      <div class="figure-row figure-row--two">
        <figure>
          <img src="/pictures/work/field-of-seeds/fos-p3-1.png" alt="Expo Culture Park, former Expo C zone" />
          <figcaption>Expo Culture Park, on the former Expo C zone.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure>
          <img src="/pictures/work/field-of-seeds/fos-p4-1.png" alt="The former UK Pavilion site, a riverside lawn" />
          <figcaption>The former UK Pavilion site, now a riverside lawn.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section
    class="portfolio-section portfolio-section--backdrop"
    style="background-image: url('/pictures/work/field-of-seeds/fos-p5-1.png')"
  >
    <div class="portfolio-section__inner">
      <div class="portfolio-section__head"><h2>Design Highlights</h2></div>
      <div class="method-architecture">
        <article>
          <small>I · Installation</small>
          <h3>A field of fluff</h3>
          <p>
            Thousands of thin optical fibers form dandelion fluff. When the wind blows, the fiber
            tips sway and light up; arranged across the lawn in large numbers, they become a field
            of dandelions.
          </p>
          <b>Wind + light</b>
        </article>
        <article>
          <small>II · Tribute & innovation</small>
          <h3>Nature and future</h3>
          <p>
            Inheriting the Seed Cathedral's theme, technology presents the beauty of natural force,
            carrying environmental and sustainable ideas and remembering the Expo.
          </p>
          <b>Memory</b>
        </article>
        <article>
          <small>III · Participation</small>
          <h3>Walk in and light up</h3>
          <p>
            Beyond the wind, people can approach a dandelion and light it themselves.
          </p>
          <b>Presence</b>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="portfolio-section">
    <div class="portfolio-section__head"><h2>The Light Dandelion</h2></div>
    <p class="portfolio-copy portfolio-copy--flush">
      Each light dandelion is a central white LED inside a 3D-printed porous core and a
      translucent shell. When lit, light passes through the porous core and lands on the shell,
      where the array of bright rectangular patches mimics dandelion seed heads.
    </p>
    <div class="figure-row figure-row--portrait">
      <figure>
        <img src="/pictures/work/field-of-seeds/fos-p6-2.png" alt="Model design draft" />
        <figcaption>Model design draft.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <img src="/pictures/work/field-of-seeds/fos-p6-1.png" alt="Light effect" />
        <figcaption>Light effect.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <img src="/pictures/work/field-of-seeds/fos-p6-3.png" alt="Prototype" />
        <figcaption>Single-unit prototype.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <div class="figure-row figure-row--uniform">
      <figure>
        <img src="/pictures/work/field-of-seeds/fos-p7-1.png" alt="Field render 1" />
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <img src="/pictures/work/field-of-seeds/fos-p8-1.png" alt="Field render 2" />
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <img src="/pictures/work/field-of-seeds/fos-p9-1.png" alt="Field render 3" />
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section
    class="portfolio-section portfolio-section--backdrop portfolio-section--backdrop--spaced"
    style="background-image: url('/pictures/work/field-of-seeds/fos-hero.png')"
  >
    <div class="portfolio-section__inner">
      <div class="portfolio-section__head"><h2>Wind and Presence</h2></div>
      <p class="portfolio-copy portfolio-copy--flush">
        The device uses an Arduino UNO board to control the lights.
      </p>
      <p class="portfolio-copy portfolio-copy--flush">
        When a “light dandelion” sways in the wind, the tilt sensor sends a signal and the “light
        dandelion” lights up; when a person approaches a “light dandelion”, the infrared sensor
        sends a signal and the “light dandelion” lights up.
      </p>
      <p class="portfolio-copy portfolio-copy--flush">
        The “light dandelions” are arranged in an array across the former UK Pavilion site. When
        the wind blows, the whole “dandelion field” flickers with the wind's rhythm; participants
        in the field can also strengthen their presence in the field through light.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="portfolio-section">
    <div class="portfolio-section__head"><h2>Making</h2></div>
    <p class="portfolio-copy portfolio-copy--flush">
      The prototype combines a 3D-printed porous core and translucent shell, a flexible metal stand
      and wire supports, felt, artificial turf, a foam base, white LEDs, an infrared sensor, a tilt
      sensor, an Arduino UNO, a breadboard and wires.
    </p>
    <div class="figure-row figure-row--uniform">
      <figure>
        <img src="/pictures/work/field-of-seeds/fos-p12-1.png" alt="The team assembling the base" />
        <figcaption>The team assembling the base</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <img src="/pictures/work/field-of-seeds/fos-p13-1.png" alt="Material 1" />
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <img src="/pictures/work/field-of-seeds/fos-p13-2.png" alt="Material 2" />
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <img src="/pictures/work/field-of-seeds/fos-p13-3.png" alt="Material 3" />
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <img src="/pictures/work/field-of-seeds/fos-p13-4.png" alt="Material 4" />
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <img src="/pictures/work/field-of-seeds/fos-p13-5.png" alt="Material 5" />
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="portfolio-section portfolio-section--closing">
    <div class="portfolio-section__label">What this is</div>
    <p class="portfolio-statement">
      A small field of light where a pavilion once stood—keeping the city's Expo memory alive in
      its only central green park.
    </p>
    <p class="portfolio-caption">
      The Field of Seeds was made with Li Tinghao and Xu Xuanzhi for the Physical Media and
      Computing course.
    </p>
  </section>
</ProjectLayout>
